(  Phenoxyethanol ................................ 99.0 - 100.0 %) Tj T*
(  Water ..................................... 0.0 - 1.0 %) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 4. FIRST-AID MEASURES) Tj T*
(  Inhalation  : Move to fresh air. Seek medical advice if discomfort persists.) Tj T*
(  Skin        : Wash with plenty of water and soap.) Tj T*
(  Eyes        : Rinse cautiously with water for several minutes.) Tj T*
(  Ingestion   : Rinse mouth. Do not induce vomiting. Seek medical advice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 5. FIRE-FIGHTING MEASURES) Tj T*
(  Suitable extinguishing media : Water spray, dry chemical, carbon dioxide, foam.) Tj T*
(  Specific hazards             : Combustion may produce carbon oxides.) Tj T*
(  Protective equipment         : Self-contained breathing apparatus.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 6. ACCIDENTAL RELEASE MEASURES) Tj T*
(  Personal precautions   : Avoid slipping hazard. Ventilate the area.) Tj T*
(  Environmental measures : Prevent entry into drains and waterways.) Tj T*
(  Clean-up methods       : Absorb with inert material and collect in containers.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 7. HANDLING AND STORAGE) Tj T*
(  Handling : Use in a well ventilated area. Keep container tightly closed.) Tj T*
(  Storage  : Store below 30 C in a dry place away from direct sunlight.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 8. EXPOSURE CONTROLS / PERSONAL PROTECTION) Tj T*
(  Engineering controls : General ventilation is normally adequate.) Tj T*
(  Eye protection       : Safety glasses with side shields.) Tj T*
(  Hand protection      : Nitrile rubber gloves.) Tj T*
(  Respiratory          : Not required under normal use.) Tj T*
